WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.614
Question fifteen.

00:00:01.614 --> 00:00:06.361
Step one: macro scan. It asks the even-parity bit.

00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:10.918
One mark. Command words: “parity bit should be”.

00:00:10.918 --> 00:00:12.627
Step two: denoise.

00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:17.279
Useful, in yellow: one zero one one zero one one.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:19.462
In cyan: “even parity”.

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:22.595
Useless: none — the stem is lean.

00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:24.304
Step three: draft.

00:00:24.304 --> 00:00:26.298
Count the ones: five.

00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:27.437
Five is odd.

00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:31.614
Even parity needs an even total, so add one.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.228
Step four: P O E.

00:00:33.228 --> 00:00:35.602
A, zero: still odd — cut.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.494
C, cannot be found: all bits given — cut.

00:00:39.494 --> 00:00:45.191
D, depends on the medium: the rule ignores the medium — cut.

00:00:45.191 --> 00:00:51.077
Step five: sanity check and lock. Five plus one is six — even.

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:53.640
So the correct answer is B.
